<title>ROMANIA: SOCCER-RETIRED ROMANIAN COACH COMMITS SUICIDE.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-RETIRED ROMANIAN COACH COMMITS SUICIDE.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Retired Romanian coach Ion Zaharia, who won the national soccer cup in 1963 with Petrolul Ploiesti, has committed suicide, police said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Zaharia, 63, plunged to his death on Tuesday from an eighth floor apartment. &quot;Zaharia had mental problems,&quot; a police spokesman said.</p>
